design: evaluate whether to migrate the Express routes in /routes/auth.js to use a middleware-based permission system or keep inline role checks.

Current implementation uses inline guards:

const express = require('express');
const router = express.Router();

router.get('/admin', (req, res) => {
  if (req.user.role !== 'admin') return res.sendStatus(403);
  // ... handle request
});

Consider trade-offs in maintainability, testability, and scalability. Recommend approach.

