design: review error handling strategy — should we use try/catch per controller or global error middleware with next(err)?

Current route:

router.get('/user/:id', async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const user = await User.findById(req.params.id);
    res.json(user);
  } catch (err) { next(err); }
});

Compare cognitive load and failure transparency. Justify preference.
